{"content":[{"c":["GERGESA*, GERGESENES*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["City on the eastern shore of the Sea of Galilee. Gergesa is near Gadara, probable site of Jesus’ miracle of healing a demon-possessed man and casting the demons into a nearby herd of swine. Though the account of this miracle in ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.8.28","r":"Matt.8.28","rawR":"Matt.8.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.8.28","value":"Matt.8.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"Matthew 8:28"}," refers to the “country of the Gergesenes” (",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"), it is most likely that Matthew used the reference to Gergesa as a regional identifier rather than a specific location. ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=GadaraGadarenes_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"GadaraGadarenes_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"GadaraGadarenes_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Gadara, Gadarenes"},"; ",{"href":"?item=GerasaGerasenes_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"GerasaGerasenes_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"GerasaGerasenes_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Gerasa, Gerasenes"},"."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"GergesaGergesenes","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Matthew 8:28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.8.28","rawQueryValue":"Matt.8.28","sourceRefExact":"Matt.8.28"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"b0c14b19cfdf3b046e085503d2f48308869160ee1cb8c5ae18ae2cbedb7d1623","sourceItemName":"GergesaGergesenes","sourceItemOrder":102,"sourceMember":"Articles/G.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"GergesaGergesenes","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Gergesa*, Gergesenes*","title":"Gergesa*, Gergesenes*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}